  "notes": [
    "Hand-maintained. The Troop Types chapter is prose, not a ruled table, so the figures are read off the chapter text and kept here for the combat engine.",
    "Read from the WAR rulebook: Infantry, Cavalry and War Beasts rank five wide with one supporting attack; Monstrous Infantry, Monstrous Cavalry, Monstrous Beasts, Swarms and Chariots rank three wide; Monstrous Infantry and Monstrous Beasts support three attacks, Swarms five; mounts make no supporting attacks; Cavalry without a split profile supports one, Monstrous Cavalry without one three; Chariots cannot support and take their Impact Hits from their own entry; no troop type grants Swiftstride.",
    "large-infantry is not a WAR troop type. One entry in the corpus still names it, so the row is kept rather than letting a lookup throw."
